A51: wake iOS's display with the first touch (no button driver yet).

Boot 32 delivered clean swipes that iOS ignored: each came right after
"A5XELTE FB: display-off request ignored (a5fb_keep_on)". iOS turns the
display off after the lock-screen idle timeout and then ignores touches,
while a5fb_keep_on keeps the picture on the panel; the A51 has no key driver
yet to press the side button. SweetFramebuffer records iOS's last
RequestPowerChange in sweet_fb_ios_display_off (even when the request is
ignored), and the A51 touch driver turns a new touch-down while it is set
into a power-key press/release through SweetHIDButtons (sweet_hid_key(0)),
swallowing that contact until it lifts.

